From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ken Russell <kbr@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 19:46:22 -0700
Subject: GL: add TexSubImage2D workaround for certain texture formats.

Add a workaround for a bug in the handling of texture uploads of certain
host-twiddled texture formats; use TexImage2D + TexSubImage2D instead of
uploading the data in the TexImage2D call. Apply this workaround to
PowerVR drivers.

(zmo note: this is an rebase for
https://chromium-review.git.corp.google.com/c/angle/angle/+/8316408.
Original author kbr asks me to land it while he is OOO. I fail to rebase
here or upload a local rebased CL to the original issue. All CL credit
should go to kbr.)

Bug: chromium:553172761
Change-Id: Ic476f67e9e814d6407a8445ec0d6ed21ec9ea46e
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8331247
Reviewed-by: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y):
- renderergl_utils.cpp: the branch orders its feature conditions differently
  (the reattachTextureToFboAfterLayerIncrease condition upstream's hunk
  anchors on sits earlier in the function here), so only the new feature
  condition is inserted, in front of the limitMaxBufferSizeTo1gb condition
  as upstream.
- src/tests/gl_tests/TextureTest.cpp: the branch's test file has diverged, so
  the new test is not carried; the branch's file is kept. Test-only.

